virglrenderer: a program pipeline that fails validation is logged, the context lives

What: when glValidateProgramPipeline says invalid, vrend logs the GL's reason (three
lines per process) and keeps the pipeline; a draw the GL then refuses is skipped like any
refused GL call (virgl-gl-error-skip-command.patch). OMACVM_VIRGL_SHADER_FAILURES=lose
keeps upstream's way: the context error ILLEGAL_PROGRAM_PIPELINE.
Why: vrend validates a new pipeline at its first draw, against the GL state of that
moment, and a failure ended the guest app's whole GL context. Apple's GL fails it while
the draw framebuffer is incomplete ("Validation Failed: Current draw framebuffer is
invalid."), which says nothing about the pipeline. The path never ran on the Mac before
virgl-shader-separable-pervertex.patch: no separable program linked (#567).
Upstream: upstream reports the context error; not sent.
Test: Tests/virgl/test-separable-pervertex.c, last row: a new separable pipeline's first
draw into a framebuffer with a 4-sample second colour buffer: one log line, no context
error, the next draw with a complete framebuffer draws; with
OMACVM_VIRGL_SHADER_FAILURES=lose the context error as upstream. Fails without this patch
(with virgl-shader-separable-pervertex.patch in).

--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -2799,8 +2799,22 @@
         * invalid pipeline; the error would stop the guest's whole context */
        GLint validation_status = GL_TRUE;
        glGetProgramPipelineiv(pipeline_id, GL_VALIDATE_STATUS, &validation_status);
-       if (!validation_status) {
+       /* OmacVM: validation judges the GL state of this moment (Apple's GL fails it while the
+        * draw framebuffer is incomplete), not the pipeline: logged, the pipeline is kept, and
+        * a draw the GL then refuses is skipped like any refused GL call */
+       if (!validation_status && vrend_shader_failures_lose()) {
            vrend_report_context_error(sub_ctx->parent, VIRGL_ERROR_CTX_ILLEGAL_PROGRAM_PIPELINE, 0);
+       } else if (!validation_status) {
+           static unsigned validate_failures;
+           if (++validate_failures <= 3) {
+               char log[256] = "";
+               glGetProgramPipelineInfoLog(pipeline_id, sizeof(log), NULL, log);
+               log[strcspn(log, "\n")] = 0;
+               virgl_error("context %d (%s): the host GL found a program pipeline invalid in "
+                           "the current state (%s), drawing on%s\n", sub_ctx->parent->ctx_id,
+                           sub_ctx->parent->debug_name, log,
+                           validate_failures == 3 ? "; further ones are not logged" : "");
+           }
        }
    }
 
